Z||000002||Alex4mula||05-23-2001||02:55 PM||||Those look sweet but I wonder how they would look with the Fiero offset if they have it. Also what about cost $$$$?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||05-23-2001||03:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>Do you mean the Compomotive CXN style ( <A HREF="http://www.usacomp.com/cxn.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.usacomp.com/cxn.htm</A>  )?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, those are the ones.  Very close.  If it had visible lug nuts, that might give it a better look.  With the hub cover, it makes it look too much like a luxury car wheel - to me at least.  And, yes, they are about $500 each - but they can custom make them in virutally any size, width, and offset.  Would probably look good painted black, with the high polished rim, but I'm hoping to find something quite a bit cheaper.  $250 per wheel is expensive IMO, but close to what I'm expecting.  Cheaper, of course, would be better. ||||reg||1
